          "type": "turn",
          "question": "my poo has been really dark, almost black and sticky, for three days and I feel light headed when i stand",
          "answer": "The urgency level for your symptoms of dark, sticky stool and light-headedness is classified as **routine**. However, it's important to note that just because no emergency pattern was identified, it does not mean your symptoms are not serious. If your symptoms worsen, or if you are experiencing severe or new symptoms, you should seek medical advice.\n\nDark, sticky stools, referred to as melena, can indicate bleeding in the upper gastrointestinal tract. This condition can sometimes lead to more significant issues, as discussed in the Gastrointestinal Bleeding guidance. Light-headedness, particularly when getting up, could relate to several factors, including blood volume changes or other underlying conditions that a clinician would want to assess.\n\nYour symptoms involve the gastrointestinal system and may also involve other systems related to dizziness and circulation. While some conditions like heart failure, migraine, or gastrointestinal issues like gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD) could potentially explain some symptoms, it is crucial to have a clinician evaluate your specific situation.\n\nPlease consider discussing these symptoms with a healthcare provider, especially if they persist or worsen.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
